  "body": "### Summary\nAs an HFR member, I want the composer's smiley picker to show **every** source of smileys: the basic ones, my forum favourites, the smileys I created, the app favourites, and a search. Smileys are a big part of HFR culture (operator). Part of #592, under umbrella #414 (M4). Operator decisions of 2026-11-07.\n\n### Analysis (#592)\n- **Basic smileys:** shown today.\n- **Forum favourites** (legacy section \"Smileys du forum\", `AnswerView.swift:1368` @ 2440d79): the account's favourites in the reply form's `#dynamic_smilies`. They are captured in fixture `R47u1` (HFR-PROTOCOL), but no parser exists yet.\n- **My own created smileys** (\"Smilies persos\" in the profile): a different set. The operator confirmed this is the \"personal smileys\" he means. **Not captured:** a Mac capture issue is opened. Never guess the page or its selectors.\n- **App favourites:** they work only through the smiley detail sheet, so they look empty. Make them discoverable: a context menu \"Ajouter aux favoris\" on any smiley, plus an empty state that explains how.\n- **Search:** it exists in code (`ReplyPosting.swift:222-254`, the `safeAreaBar` at `SmileyPickerView.swift:27`), but the operator did not see it. Make it visible, for example with `.searchable`. Reproduce on the Mac first.\n\n### Scope of this issue\n1. Parse `#dynamic_smilies` into a model (`HFRParsing`, pure function, differential test against `R47u1`). Show it as the section \"Smileys du forum\".\n2. Make app favourites discoverable (context menu, empty-state text).\n3. Make search visible.\n4. Lay the picker out as clear sections: basic, forum favourites, mine (once captured), app favourites, with search on top.\n5. \"Mes smileys\": add it once the capture lands. If it is not captured when this PR is ready, ship 1-4 and keep this part open as `Refs`.\n\n### Mac check\n- All sections are visible with an account that has forum favourites.\n- Adding an app favourite.\n- Search.\n- Light and dark mode, Dynamic Type XL.\n\nRouting: Sonnet 5.5 writes, Opus 5.5 reviews. Claimed for `ext/francoisgn-composer-c`.",
