   "body": "## Mac check (mac/m2-lead repro) 2026-11-07: the search bar **is** shown\n\n**Build** `f9901d9` (origin/dev-swift). **Devices**: iPhone 18 Pro simulator, iOS 27.0, portrait; iPad Pro 13-inch (M5) simulator, iOS 27.0, landscape. Logged in. The composer was always cancelled, never sent. Screenshots checked by eye. Harness note: the build was signed ad hoc (`CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=-`) instead of unsigned, so the login could use the keychain.\n\n| Where | Search bar | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| iPhone, new MP composer → Smileys | ✅ visible, hittable | **At the bottom** of the sheet, below a large empty area: \"Rechercher un smiley…\", the 🔍 button and the \"Tous les mots clés\" toggle. The keyboard is down when the picker opens |\n| iPhone, reply composer → Smileys | ✅ same place | |\n| iPad, new MP composer → Smileys | ✅ visible | Bottom of the form sheet |\n| iPhone, tap the field and type 2 letters | ✅ the bar rides up on the keyboard; the hint \"Saisissez au moins 3 caractères…\" shows | No search was run (3+ characters not typed) |\n\nSo the bar exists and works on this build. It is easy to miss: it sits at the very bottom of a tall sheet, away from the smileys, with a grey field on a white sheet and no title. The picker also shows only \"Smileys basiques\" (35) and \"Favoris de l'app\" (0, \"Aucun favori dans l'app pour le moment.\").\n\nThis supports moving the search to the top (`.searchable` or a bar under the title), as point 3 of the issue says. No bug was found that would hide the bar on this build. A device check (Dynamic Type XL, small iPhone) is still owed with the fix.\n",
